--- !u!114 &349075700
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 349075696}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 30e8e37d88289204784a0442b3c88612, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  steps:
  - Connect (220 VAC) terminal and the neutral path (N) of all used modules to the
    (220 VAC) terminal and the neutral path (N) of the main board.
  - Connect an Ethernet cable from the PV Solar Panel (Comm. Out) to the Main Control
    Board module (Comm. In).
  - Connect (+VE) and (-VE) terminals of the PV solar panel output module to (1)
    and (3) terminals of Rheostat 800-ohm module.
  - Release the emergency stop button on the main board.
  - Raise the circuit breaker (C.B) of the main board.
  - Switch on the main board ON/OFF switch.
  - Release the emergency button of the PV Solar Panel.
  - Switch on the PV Solar Panel ON/OFF.
  - Switch the Run/Stop selector to Run state.
  - Open the control software on the connected PC.
  - Navigate to the "Measurements Graph" tab.
  - Select the graph of the DC Current vs. DC voltage
  - Gradually decrease the rheostat's resistance (increase the load) by turning its
    knob counter-clockwise. Observe that the current increases while the voltage
    drops.
  - Switch to the software monitor again. The I-V characteristic curve will be drawn
    on the graph corresponding to the recorded points.
  popups:
  - afterStep: 11
    text: Always ensure emergency buttons are released before powering on any module.
  - afterStep: 3
    text: You can choose "Enable" button and use the slider to adjust the light dimming
      power of the solar panel from the software and observe the voltage and current
      values.
  - afterStep: 14
    text: When you decrease the resistance (increase the load), you will notice that
      the current consumption increases, resulting in a voltage drop and vice versa.
  - afterStep: 14
    text: "Note that you can:\nExport all recorded measurements to an Excel sheet
      by clicking the \"Export Data\" icon.\r\nSave the screen by pressing the \"Save
      Screen\" icon.\r\nClear the graph using the \"Clear\" icon\r"
  stepItemPrefab: {fileID: 6570533322573217691, guid: cd25d304eaf4809488e7c6b299d13404, type: 3}
  contentParent: {fileID: 349075697}
