--- !u!114 &889749493
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 889749491}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 30e8e37d88289204784a0442b3c88612, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  steps:
  - Connect (220 VAC) terminal and the neutral path (N) of all used modules to the
    (220 VAC) terminal and the neutral path (N) of the main board.
  - Connect an Ethernet cable from the Main frame (Comm. Out) to the wind mill module
    (Comm. In)
  - Connect the (+VE) and (-VE) terminals of the Battery 24V module to the (+VE)
    and (-VE) Battery Input terminals of the Off-Grid Inverter module.
  - Connect the (+VE) and (-VE) terminals of the DC LED Lamp module to the (+VE)
    and (-VE) Battery Input terminals of the Off-Grid Inverter module.
  - Release the emergency stop button on the main board
  - Raise the circuit breaker (C.B) of the main board.
  - Switch on the main board ON/OFF switch.
  - Switch on the off-grid inverter using the power switch located beneath the device.
  - Connect the (+VE) and (-VE) AC Output terminals of the Off-Grid Inverter module
    to the (+VE) and (-VE) terminals of the AC Lamp module.
  - Connect (L1), (L2), and (L3) terminals of the Generator Output from the wind
    turbine module to the (L1), (L2), and (L3) input terminals of the Full Bridge
    Rectifier.
  - Connect the (+VE) and (-VE) output terminals of the Rectifier module to the (+VE)
    and (-VE) DC input terminals of the Off-Grid Inverter module.
  - Release the emergency button on the wind mill
  - Raise the circuit breaker (C.B) of the wind mill.
  - Switch on the wind mill ON/OFF.
  - Gradually increase the wind mill speed in small increments.
  - Switch to the software monitor.
  - Connect (L) and (N) terminals of the AC Input of the Off-Grid Inverter module
    to the (220 VAC) terminal and the neutral path (N) of the main board.
  - Switch to the software monitor again.
  - You have finished! You can now select another experiment.
  popups:
  - afterStep: 8
    text: "\u201CYou will notice that the battery power displays a negative sign.
      This indicates that the battery is actively discharging to supply energy to
      both the DC load and the Off-Grid Inverter.\u201D"
  - afterStep: 9
    text: "Note: \u201CAfter adding the AC lamp, the current drawn from the battery
      increased significantly. You can connect additional AC loads in parallel to
      observe the system's response to higher power demands."
  - afterStep: 15
    text: "\u201CAs soon as the wind turbine is activated, current sharing occurs
      between the battery and the turbine.\u201D"
  - afterStep: 17
    text: "\u201CNow, you can observe that the battery shows a positive current,
      indicating it is being charged by the AC grid.\u201D"
  - afterStep: 18
    text: 'Attention when you finish the experiment, perform the following steps
      in order:

      Disconnect the AC and DC loads.

      Disconnect the AC input
      source.

      Disconnect the wind Turbine.

      Finally disconnect the battery.'
  stepItemPrefab: {fileID: 6570533322573217691, guid: cd25d304eaf4809488e7c6b299d13404, type: 3}
  contentParent: {fileID: 889749492}
