--- !u!114 &1907595364
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1907595362}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 30e8e37d88289204784a0442b3c88612, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  steps:
  - 'Connect (220 VAC) terminal and the neutral path (N) of all used modules to the
    (220 VAC) terminal and the neutral path (N) of the main board. '
  - Connect an Ethernet cable from the Main frame (Comm. Out) to the wind mill module
    (Comm. In)
  - Connect (L1), (L2), and (L3) terminals of the Generator Output from the wind
    mill module to the (L1), (L2), and (L3) input terminals of the Full Bridge Rectifier
    module.
  - Connect the (+VE) and (-VE) output terminals of the Rectifier module to the (+VE)
    and (-VE) DC input terminals of the MPPT charger controller module.
  - Connect the (+VE) and (-VE) terminals of the Battery 24V module to the (+VE)
    and (-VE) Battery terminals of the MPPT charger controller module.
  - Connect the (+VE) and (-VE) DC Load terminals of the MPPT charger controller
    module to the (+VE) and (-VE) terminals of the DC Halogen Lamp module.
  - Release the emergency stop button on the main board
  - Raise the circuit breaker (C.B) of the main board.
  - Switch on the main board ON/OFF switch.
  - Operate the DC load from the MPPT charge control.
  - 'Release the emergency button on the wind turbine '
  - Raise the circuit breaker (C.B) of the wind turbine.
  - Switch on the wind mill ON/OFF.
  - Enable the generator output enable/ disable switch to allow the voltage to reach
    the input of the rectifier module and adjust the emulator to minimum speed.
  - Gradually increase the wind mill speed in small increments.
  - Switch to the software monitor.
  - Navigate to the "System" tab to observe the results
  - You have finished! You can now select another experiment.
  popups:
  - afterStep: 5
    text: Always ensure emergency buttons are released before powering on any module.
  - afterStep: 9
    text: You will notice that the battery power displays a negative sign. This indicates
      that the battery is actively discharging to supply energy to both the DC load
      and the MPPT charge controller
  - afterStep: 14
    text: As the turbine speed increases, the current and voltage output from the
      turbine rise. The battery power reading becomes positive, confirming that the
      battery is now being charged.
  - afterStep: 16
    text: "Attention when you finish the experiment, perform the following steps
      in order: \r\n1)\tDisconnect the DC load. \r\n2)\tDisconnect the wind Turbine.
      \r\n3)\tFinally disconnect the battery. "
  stepItemPrefab: {fileID: 6570533322573217691, guid: cd25d304eaf4809488e7c6b299d13404, type: 3}
  contentParent: {fileID: 1907595363}
